    kind: work_item  # d2b9
    title: "test-only-reachability gate cannot see repository scripts: production_source_files globs packages/*/src only, so confidence_sites' four functions (called from scripts/check-confidence-sites) fail the cron full-suite as test-only"  # d2b9
    status: todo_hard  # d2b9
    priority: 2  # d2b9
    parent:  # d2b9
    tags:  # d2b9
    - ci_infrastructure  # d2b9
    - analysis_quality  # d2b9
    isbefore: []  # d2b9
    duplicate_of: []  # d2b9
    not_duplicate_of: []  # d2b9
    pr_ref:  # d2b9
    description: "## Symptom (cron full-suite, dev @ f7c93e494e, 2026-10-16 18:33 EDT, pipeline 4872)\n`self-tree-validation` step fails via `check-test-only-reachability`:\n```\nFAIL: 4 function(s) are newly reachable only from their own tests:\n  + packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/confidence_sites.py::baseline_document\n  + packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/confidence_sites.py::compare_to_baseline\n  + packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/confidence_sites.py::load_baseline\n  + packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/confidence_sites.py::scan_tree\nWire it to production or retire it. The baseline is shrink-only and may not be raised to accommodate this.\n```\n## Root cause (structural, not dead code)\nThose four functions ARE wired to production: `scripts/check-confidence-sites` (pre-commit + CI gate shipped in the 9.1.0 cycle) imports and calls them. But `hypergumbo_core/test_only_reachability.py::production_source_files` is `root.glob(\"packages/*/src/**/*.py\")` -- repository scripts are extensionless, so a call from `scripts/*` is invisible to the gate and the only visible callers are the tests. `check_id_construction.py` sits in `.ci/test-only-reachability-baseline.json` for exactly the same reason (its production caller is `scripts/check-id-construction`). Any future `scripts/check-*` backed by a core module will trip this gate on its first cron.\n## Fix (general)\nTreat repository scripts as production sources: in `production_source_files`, add files directly under `scripts/` whose first line is a Python shebang (and `scripts/**/*.py`), and let `collect_production_references` scan them. Then the four `confidence_sites` functions are production-reachable, the `check_id_construction` entries fall out of the cohort, and the baseline SHRINKS (allowed; rewrite it with `--write-baseline`, which needs a self-analysis map). Alternative if scripts must stay out of the map: a `script_entry` set-aside reason computed from an AST scan of `scripts/*` imports, alongside the existing `carries_a_decorator` / `dispatch_binding` / `not_gated_kind` set-asides.\n## Done when\nCron full-suite `self-tree-validation` is green on dev; baseline rewritten (smaller); a unit test pins that a function called only from a shebang script under `scripts/` is not test-only."  # d2b9
    fields: {}  # d2b9
